1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,433
Why do cells bother with fermentation?

2
00:00:02,883 --> 00:00:06,681
It regenerates NAD+, so glycolysis can keep going.

3
00:00:07,131 --> 00:00:09,669
Muscle cells turn pyruvate into lactate.

4
00:00:09,919 --> 00:00:13,098
Yeast turns it into ethanol and CO2.

5
00:00:13,348 --> 00:00:16,697
Either way, only the 2 ATP from glycolysis.

6
00:00:17,147 --> 00:00:19,366
So which kind happens in muscle cells?

7
00:00:19,616 --> 00:00:21,280
Lactic acid fermentation.

8
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:24,738
Every card and question cites the notes it came from.

9
00:00:24,988 --> 00:00:26,545
Try StudyProofs on your own.
